WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:01.080
- Hi, I'm Rie.

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.880
Welcome back to "Make it Fancy".

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:05.910
Before we begin, we got
some cool new merch.

00:00:05.910 --> 00:00:09.840
You can check it out
at shopmakeitfancy.com.

00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.970
Let's see what I'm making fancy today.

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.610
- Hey Rie, it's Katie and
today I'm challenging you

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:17.160
to make rice crispy treats fancy.

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.110
I used to eat these all
the time growing up.

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:20.580
I'd have 'em after soccer games.

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:22.140
They definitely remind me of being young.

00:00:22.140 --> 00:00:24.930
I would love to see you
make them more fancy

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:25.860
and kind of elevate them.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:28.413
So I can't wait to see
how you make it fancy.

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:31.290
- Rice Krispies Treats.

00:00:31.290 --> 00:00:34.380
This is a limited Make it Fancy edition.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:35.670
It's only existing here.

00:00:35.670 --> 00:00:36.540
It's so cute.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:38.850
Rice crispy with marshmallow,

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.613
it's a little too sweet for me.

00:00:43.301 --> 00:00:45.090
Oh. It's not bad.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:46.230
I like the texture.

00:00:46.230 --> 00:00:48.540
It's gooey, but it's still crispy.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.580
This is better than I expected.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:53.883
As always, I'm excited to make it fancy.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:57.840
All right. Here's what I got.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:01.440
Marshmallows, sprinkles,
strawberry chocolate,

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:05.640
white chocolate, milk chocolate,
cocoa powder, cacao nibs,

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.880
butter, cream cheese, and heavy cream.

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:13.230
From the pantry I got
canola oil, coconut oil,

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:18.150
vanilla extract, salt, food
coloring, and powdered sugar.

00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:20.010
Let's get started.

00:01:20.010 --> 00:01:21.033
Make it fancy.

00:01:23.070 --> 00:01:27.990
I have three cups of heavy cream
heated up just on the boil.

00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:28.948
It's nice and hot.

00:01:28.948 --> 00:01:31.367
Add rice crispy treats.

00:01:31.367 --> 00:01:34.500
Simmer this about 15 minutes and reduce it

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.390
to one and a half cup.

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:37.919
15 minutes later.

00:01:37.919 --> 00:01:39.000
- [Producer] Rie, we have another

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.890
special rice crispy treats package.

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.783
- Throw them.
- [Producer] Yeah, sure.

00:01:43.898 --> 00:01:45.481
- Oh, it's so cute.

00:01:46.667 --> 00:01:47.983
Me.

00:01:47.983 --> 00:01:51.900
Strain it. Put this in a
refrigerator at least one hour.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:54.120
So it get very cold.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:56.460
I have six inch cake bun.

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.760
Spray oil so it doesn't stick.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:03.300
And I have rice crispy treats,

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.050
process this in the food processor.

00:02:05.970 --> 00:02:06.803
Woohoo.

00:02:09.726 --> 00:02:11.097
Looks nice.

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:12.300
Set this aside.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:13.500
Move on to next step.

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.680
Four tablespoon of butter, melt it.

00:02:16.680 --> 00:02:20.400
One cup of mini marshmallow,
melt this completely.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:22.980
This marshmallow gave me a flashback

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:25.200
of our marshmallow episode.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.370
Our producer Cyrus told me
alligator likes marshmallows,

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:32.730
but alligator is almost
like a dinosaur, right?

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:36.540
Alligator was there before
marshmallow was invented

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.970
who did it to them?

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:41.209
So this is completely melted.

00:02:41.209 --> 00:02:44.490
Add cocoa powder, one table spoon.

00:02:44.490 --> 00:02:47.850
I like using cocoa powder
and of course, cocoa nibs

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:50.760
so we can kind of balance
it out, the sweetness.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:55.140
Crushed rice crispy, two
table spoon of cacao nibs,

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:55.980
mix it.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:58.140
I think it looks very appetizing.

00:02:58.140 --> 00:02:59.940
It's gooey and chocolate-y.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:02.250
I want to make sure
everything is evenly coated.

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:03.747
It looks great.

00:03:03.747 --> 00:03:06.000
You put this in a pan.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:07.140
This might be a little hot

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:09.120
so I'm gonna start with the spatula.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:14.120
You press to the mold
and cover the bottom part

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:17.070
then you want to make it even thickness.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:20.460
I'm going to put this in
the freezer about 15 minutes

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:21.690
so it firm up.

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:25.710
I have one half cup
chilled rice crispy treats

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.750
infused heavy cream.

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:29.820
I'm going to whip this by hand.

00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:32.100
I saw "America's Test kitchen".

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:37.080
The fastest way to whip cream
by hand was just doing this.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.240
I feel like my arm get tired

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:41.340
so I kind of want to move around.

00:03:41.340 --> 00:03:42.750
All right. This is looking good.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.580
I got the medium stiff peaks.

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:45.750
I'm going to chill this.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:49.440
One pound cream cheese,
put it in the stand mixer.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:54.090
Half cup of powdered sugar.

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:57.573
And using paddle attachment,
mix it until smooth.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:01.530
I'm gonna scrape the side.

00:04:01.530 --> 00:04:04.020
Half tablespoon of vanilla extract,

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:06.303
quarter teaspoon of salt.

00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:11.460
All right. This looks nice.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:14.850
So I have this cream cheese mixture here

00:04:14.850 --> 00:04:19.320
combine one and half
cup rice crispy treats

00:04:19.320 --> 00:04:21.060
infused whipped cream.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.890
I like the texture.

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:24.330
Jiggle jiggle.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:26.310
Using spatula, fold that in.

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:28.290
I think it's gonna be delicious.

00:04:28.290 --> 00:04:31.670
- [Producer] Rie, are you
familiar with the elf trio?

00:04:31.670 --> 00:04:32.616
- Do they have name?

00:04:32.616 --> 00:04:35.469
- [Producer] One is named
Snap, one is named Crackle.

00:04:35.469 --> 00:04:37.619
- Another one is Gooey.

00:04:37.619 --> 00:04:39.600
- [Producer] Pop.
- Pop.

00:04:39.600 --> 00:04:41.820
Elf is always look like a grandpa, right?

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:46.380
And I'm going to divide
this mixture into three.

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:48.810
I still have a little
bit whipped cream left,

00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:52.933
but I'm going to use it for
later and let's get fancy.

00:04:52.933 --> 00:04:55.600
(piano playing)

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.620
I melted three different chocolate,

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.470
milk chocolate, white chocolate,
and strawberry chocolate.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:20.430
And now I'm going to mix into
the cream cheese mixture.

00:05:20.430 --> 00:05:23.700
First, I'm going to mix
with milk chocolate.

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:26.520
Mix well, looks good.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:30.360
Pour this into the mold with crust.

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:35.360
Use small offset spatula,
smooth the surface.

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:37.410
Freeze this about five minutes.

00:05:37.410 --> 00:05:40.380
This one was in freezer and it it's firm.

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:43.080
Next layer, white chocolate.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:47.370
Again, using offset spatula
and making even layer.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:48.450
All right. It looks great.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.840
Put this in the freezer for five minutes.

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:54.510
So it's firmed up, make the third layer.

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:57.600
And I'm going to add a
little bit of food coloring

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:02.190
because when you mix with
cream cheese and strawberry

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:03.840
it's get very pale.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:06.750
So I just want to make
a little bit vibrant.

00:06:06.750 --> 00:06:09.434
The strawberry chocolate, it's popular

00:06:09.434 --> 00:06:12.150
'cause like there's
Pocky strawberry flavor.

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.680
It's similar to Neapolitan.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:16.983
It has chocolate and white and strawberry.

00:06:16.983 --> 00:06:19.590
Okay using offset spatula.

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:22.770
Pan is getting heavy. It's very full.

00:06:22.770 --> 00:06:25.620
Refrigerate this at least six hours.

00:06:25.620 --> 00:06:28.860
I have two parchment paper.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:33.450
Put rice crispy and using
rolling pin you just roll it.

00:06:33.450 --> 00:06:36.960
You want to roll maybe
like half the thickness.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:40.260
- [Producer] In 2015, somebody made

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:43.140
the world's biggest rice krispies treat.

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:44.560
Guess the weight.

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:45.807
- 250 pounds.

00:06:45.807 --> 00:06:46.640
- [Producer] 11,327 pounds.

00:06:48.930 --> 00:06:49.890
- That's so off.

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:53.400
I have a strawberry shaped cookie cutter.

00:06:53.400 --> 00:06:55.020
It's very sticky.

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:57.603
So I'm going to use this, the plunger.

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:03.740
So I am making strawberry
shaped rice crispy treats.

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.870
I think Katie will like it.

00:07:06.870 --> 00:07:09.090
I think Katie likes cute stuff.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:12.750
I'm going to make more and
I'm excited to show Katie

00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:14.490
what the final product look like.

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:18.480
I have all rice crispy treats strawberry

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:23.310
and I'm going to cover with
melted strawberry chocolate

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:24.390
with coconut oil.

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:26.880
And I'm going to freeze
this for five minutes.

00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:27.990
Chocolate is set.

00:07:27.990 --> 00:07:29.970
But it doesn't look like strawberry,

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:33.240
so I'm going to make it
look more like strawberry.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:35.700
And this is just a melted white chocolate.

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:38.220
Make a tiny dots.

00:07:38.220 --> 00:07:40.350
White chocolate is a little bit sticky

00:07:40.350 --> 00:07:42.210
and it's kind of giving me a streak

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:44.610
so I try not to move too much

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:48.246
to make it perfect strawberry seeds

00:07:48.246 --> 00:07:53.246
and twisting the toothpick so
it doesn't have any streak.

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:57.510
My hands used to be very shaky,

00:07:57.510 --> 00:08:01.470
but now I feel like I
gained a steady hands.

00:08:01.470 --> 00:08:03.630
Chill this and get ready to decorate.

00:08:03.630 --> 00:08:08.630
So I go inspired from Korean lunchbox cake

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:13.770
and I have this like paper lunchbox.

00:08:13.770 --> 00:08:15.300
Put pink tissue.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:18.450
I'm using offset spatula to unmold it.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:21.150
All right. And I'm going
to decorate the cake

00:08:21.150 --> 00:08:25.690
with strawberry shaped rice crispy treats.

00:08:25.690 --> 00:08:29.550
And I have some pastel color sprinkles.

00:08:29.550 --> 00:08:33.420
Rice crispy treats infused whipped cream.

00:08:33.420 --> 00:08:36.390
This is actually inspired
by the baker in San Jose.

00:08:36.390 --> 00:08:37.440
Her name is Tina Lee.

00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:39.000
Her cake was really pretty.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:41.580
I'm piping with star piping tip.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:45.570
I'm adding my final touches
and make a strawberry top

00:08:45.570 --> 00:08:46.740
with white chocolate.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:48.769
And I'm going to use toothpick

00:08:48.769 --> 00:08:53.400
to make little strawberry top decoration.

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:55.476
And we are done.

00:08:55.476 --> 00:08:58.059
(gentle music)

00:09:06.180 --> 00:09:09.300
Rice crispy treats lunchbox cake.

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:10.533
Very cute and fancy.

